  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ashish Kumar vs The State Of Jharkhand on 21 December, 2022 Author: Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi Bench: Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi Cr.M.P. No. 4525 of 2022 Ashish Kumar @ Ashish Kumar Modi ..... ... Petitione Versus 1. The State of Jharkhand 2. Dhaneshwar Prasad Hembram ..... ... Opposite Partie -------- Coram : Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi ------ For the Petitioner : Ms Sonal Sodhani, Advocate. For the State : Mrs. Priya Shrestha, Spl.P.P. ------ 02/ 21.12.2022",
    "facts": "This petition has been filed for quashing of the entire criminal proceeding including the order dated 12.03.2020, passed by the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Dumka, in connection with Complaint Case (OCR) No. 665/2020, by which, cognizance for the offence under Section 3(1)(ZZ)(viii) of Food Safety and Standard Act, has been taken against the petitioner, pending in that court.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that Section 3(1)(ZZ)(viii) of Food Safety and Standard Act is a definition section with regard to the said Act. She submits that the penal provision is Section 59 of the said Act. Learned Spl.P.P., appearing for the State has tried to justify the impugned order passed by the learned court and submits that after looking into the records, the aforesaid order has been passed.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that Section 3(1)(ZZ)(viii) of Food Safety and Standard Act is a definition section with regard to the said Act. She submits that the penal provision is Section 59 of the said Act. Learned Spl.P.P., appearing for the State has tried to justify the impugned order passed by the learned court and submits that after looking into the records, the aforesaid order has been passed.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
